<BaseLayout title="Engine compartment overview">
  <h1>Engine compartment overview</h1>
  <p>This page uses Volvo's own 2021 S60 engine-compartment illustration to identify routine service points. It is a location guide, not a substitute for checking the actual vehicle: Volvo explicitly notes that the layout can vary by model and engine variant.</p>
  <figure class="reference-photo">
    <a href="https://www.volvocars.com/media/support-content/img4b4a330b573d9c4ec0a801524b07b5d5_1_--_--_VOICEpnghigh.png" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
      <img src="https://www.volvocars.com/media/support-content/img4b4a330b573d9c4ec0a801524b07b5d5_1_--_--_VOICEpnghigh.png" alt="Volvo 2021 S60 engine compartment overview with six numbered service-point callouts" loading="lazy" />
    </a>
    <figcaption>Volvo 2021 S60 owner's information — engine compartment overview. Open image for full size. Image © Volvo Cars.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <h2>Numbered components</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Coolant expansion tank.</strong> Check level only under the conditions described in the owner's manual. Never open the cap while the system is hot or pressurized.</li>
    <li><strong>Brake-fluid reservoir.</strong> Located on the driver's side. Brake-fluid work is safety-critical; a falling level can indicate pad wear or a leak and should not simply be topped up without investigation.</li>
    <li><strong>Washer-fluid filler.</strong> Use washer fluid with freeze protection appropriate for the season. Volvo notes that the washer system can also supply the headlamp cleaning system where fitted.</li>
    <li><strong>Fusebox / central electrical unit.</strong> Use the fuse chart supplied for the exact vehicle. Never replace a fuse with a higher amperage rating.</li>
    <li><strong>Air filter.</strong> The housing and intake layout can differ between engine variants. Confirm the correct filter and service procedure by VIN.</li>
    <li><strong>Engine-oil filler.</strong> Use the oil grade specified for the installed engine code. Add oil gradually and verify the level using Volvo's electronic measurement procedure.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>Important safety notes from Volvo</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The radiator cooling fan may start or continue running automatically for up to approximately six minutes after the engine is switched off.</li>
    <li>Volvo warns that the ignition system operates at very high, hazardous voltage. Set the vehicle electrical system to ignition position 0 before work in the engine compartment.</li>
    <li>Do not touch spark plugs or ignition coils with the electrical system in ignition position II or while the engine is warm.</li>
    <li>Volvo recommends that engine cleaning be entrusted to a workshop; there is a fire risk if the engine is hot.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Variant note</h2>
  <p>The image is the 2021 S60 owner's-manual overview, not a photograph of every engine option. T5 and T6 gasoline engines have different induction hardware; T8 Recharge adds high-voltage hybrid components and additional safety requirements. The illustration does not identify those components or authorize work on them. Compare the image with the actual engine bay and VIN-specific service information.</p>
